{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head 906dc884e1ef3ad165fa2579dbda2727228103bb, under review request #23045 and Hugh's implementation request #23017.\n\n1. Add the required concurrent incorporation proof. cmd/gs/incorporation_test.go proves a second sequential call refuses and counts one receipt, but no new test races incorporation attempts. Existing TestMergeGuardSerializesConcurrentApprovalUse models a Git receipt-ref reservation; the new path deliberately creates no such ref. Existing merge-process tests exercise ordinary merges under a shared local lock, not the stated cross-machine resident/idempotency guarantee. Conditions 3 and 5 explicitly require concurrent attempts to leave one receipt and mutation-sensitive coverage of every guard. Exercise two independently planned incorporation submissions against one resident, with a deterministic barrier ensuring both passed the initial no-receipt check. Cover identical receipt bodies and differing --text or observed pre-heads. Assert one durable receipt, at most one successful append, replay or a named conflict for the second, unchanged target/HEAD/index/worktree, and correct landed closure. Demonstrate that removing or varying the deterministic approval key makes the proof fail. Keep this repair on the existing commitment.\n\nArchitecture: affected layers 5 (Workroom receipt interpretation and profile/cache contract) and 7 (merge planning and CLI composition). The exact head changes the receipt contract, documents it in docs/reference/architecture.md, and publishes that page as candidate artifact ba9cb0e6. Layer 5 still reads no Git and prior incorporation confers no cross-author retirement authority. Layer 7 measures reachability and constructs one empty-plan assertion. Kernel/signature and transport contracts remain unchanged. The profile advances to workroom-fold@25 and the prior-profile cache regression passes.\n\nSecurity: examined independent ratified approval, implementer identity, destination/hold validation, receipt reach, nonempty-plan refusal, admission and idempotency boundaries. No demonstrated new authority bypass. Independent resident-boundary probes withdrew the approval and then the reporting artifact immediately before /v0/submit; both were refused by admission, with no landed receipt. The documented target-force-push window is a consequence of the no-ref-transaction simplification explicitly commissioned in #23017. Single-use across independent concurrent clients remains unproven by this head's tests, so I cannot approve condition 3 on the sequential test alone.\n\nAuthority reconciliation: do not claim that the older design note supplies all four facts of SKILL.md's authority-bearing decision chain. Its source request e1bede35 explicitly says design only and do not implement; candidate artifact #17273 likewise says adopts nothing. Independent review e093dd4d, sealed delivery #17282 and live fresh successor #17283 establish reviewed delivery, not authorization to implement from that older chain. This head rests instead on Hugh's new direct implementation commission #23017, which explicitly chooses the authority argument and two simplifications. Keep that distinction clear in the next review request; I am not certifying the four-fact follow-on route for the older note.\n\nSimplification: the single receipt and shared planner branch match the commissioned scope. Cut repetitive explanatory comments (especially recordMergeIncorporation and validIncorporation) to the invariants the code must preserve. The recordMergeIncorporation comment currently promises racing attempts replay identical acts; the reference page more accurately allows an idempotency conflict for differing text or observations. Align the brief comment with that behavior while adding the proof.\n\nValidation: focused incorporation tests in cmd/gs, internal/mergeplan and internal/workroom pass; TestReceiptAccountingRejectsPriorProjectionCaches passes; both changed merge/merge-plan runnable reference examples pass; git diff --check passes; reviewed worktree clean at 906dc884. Independent withdrawal probes were external Go overlays, with results retained under /var/folders/2x/wylr59t17ds36l1l7ng25y7w0000gn/T/codex-incorporation-review-1ro8makm. I did not change repository source or repeat the author's reported full-suite run. Publish repaired exact-head artifacts citing this verdict and request fresh review.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:9486fc963f3e25b9c3177b8dc8d65a485a856a2f","head":"906dc884e1ef3ad165fa2579dbda2727228103bb","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:62802726a5ea229bc5718eeaeb53b00e00c334f6\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:62802726a5ea229bc5718eeaeb53b00e00c334f6","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}